146
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Scoutmastership in seven minutes or less.

147
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Scouting is a nationwide movement

148
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
of about 2.8 million youth

149
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
and 1.3 million adults,

150
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
And the whole thing is all written down.

151
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
It's been around for a century

152
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
and it's defined in policies and procedures

153
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
and manuals and training

154
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:58,000
and all kinds of good resources that are out there.

155
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,000
It's not really subject to an individual's understanding

156
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
or the way that they would like to invent it

157
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
or reinvent it or apply it.

158
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:09,000
There's some pretty cut and dried stuff,

159
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
And the reason that it's cut and dried

160
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
is because it works.

161
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
I liken this to getting some kind of

162
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,000
new electronic gadget or power tool

163
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,000
or something like that.

164
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
Everybody's probably done that.

165
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
You know we send away for it

166
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
and we get it in the mail,

167
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
or we go to the store and we pick it up

168
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
And if you're like me,

169
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,000
the first thing you want to do is unwrap that new toy

170
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,000
and start playing with it.

171
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
You know we plug it in, power it up

172
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
and forge ahead right,

173
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
And then when something doesn't work

174
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
like we think it should,

175
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,000
we kind of get frustrated

176
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
and we assume one or two things.

177
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
We assume that the toy is broken

178
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
and maybe we just throw it back in the box

179
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
and forget about it,

180
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Or we invent some kind of ingenious workaround

181
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
to avoid the supposed flaw in the tool

182
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
or the toy or the gadget

183
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
And especially the kind of personality

184
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
that becomes a scout leader,

185
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Because we've. you know

186
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
it takes a bit of an ego.

187
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
It takes some self-assurance and confidence.

188
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
It takes somebody who is going to forge ahead

189
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
and who is going to make things happen.

190
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
You know, back to the toy.

191
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
after we've grown dissatisfied

192
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
with the way that it works and everything,

193
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
as a last resort we might fish the manual

194
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
that came along with it out of the trash

195
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
and start reading impatiently.

196
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Are you following me here?

197
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Has this happened to you.

198
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
It's happened to me.

199
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
We might read that manual kind of impatiently

200
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
after we get through the seven different languages

201
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
and all the warnings and everything like that

202
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
and get to the point where they start talking about

203
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
how to use the thing

204
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
and we may eventually find an answer

205
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
to the problem that we were having with it.

206
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
We may find out: oh well, you know,

207
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
you have to do this before you do this,

208
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Or you have to charge it up for 12 hours,

209
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Or oh, it could be any one of a hundred things.

210
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
And that might even make us more disgruntled

211
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
or more upset with the whole thing

212
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
than we were when we first found out

213
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
that it didn't work the way that we had hoped it worked.

214
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
And it can cause a real disconnect in our thinking

215
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
because we've got our new toy

216
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
and it doesn't work the way that we think it should work.

217
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
You know it works the way it was designed to work,

218
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
but not necessarily the way we think it should work.

219
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
So you know we're going to either take it back

220
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
and get our money back,

221
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
or we're sheepishly going to admit

222
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
that our first assumptions weren't exactly correct

223
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
and now we will make an uneasy peace

224
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
with our new toy or tool

225
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
and it will go to work for us.

226
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
So you know where I'm going with this right,

227
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Because scouting is a lot like this.

228
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
It's something that we come to and we think:

229
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,000
well, you know, if we were scouts when we were youth,

230
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,000
we have a set of assumptions based on our experiences

231
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,000
that we're going to work with.

232
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
If we volunteer to become scouts as adults,

233
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
you know our son gets involved

234
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
and then you volunteer to become a scout as an adult

235
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
And of course you don't want to look

236
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
as though you don't know anything.

237
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
So you make some assumptions and you move on

238
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
and you've heard different things

239
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
about Scoutmasters and scouts

240
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
and the way it's supposed to work,

241
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
just in the general culture.

242
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
And when things don't work

243
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
the way that we think they ought to work,

244
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
we get a little disgruntled

245
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
and we might start changing things

246
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:26,000
and trying to fix things that don't need fixing.

247
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,000
And as a last resort, we fish out the manual

248
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:33,000
and we read and we find out what to do

249
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
to make things work properly.

250
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I'll give you an example.

251
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Let's take a look at two Scout requirements

252
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
For the Scout badge. number 7 says:

253
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
you understand and agree to live by

254
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
the Scout oath or promise

255
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
the Scout law, the motto and slogan in the outdoor code.

256
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
That's what it says

257
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
For the tenderfoot rank. the same number,

258
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
number 7, says: repeat from memory

259
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
and explain in your own words

